Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-25-2000||04:48 PM||||Did you press "Ctrl-V" in your message?  That's what actually gets the pic from Cliffs files to your post.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||01-25-2000||07:50 PM||||Yep, Monkeyman is right. After you have posted the image (and got the "Upload Successful!" message), you need to press CTL-V inside your forum message. To re-use an image you have already posted (actually, try this now):<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Start your message in this forum<BR><LI>Type your message, <B>do not press <I>Submit Reply</I> just yet</B><BR><LI>Open PIP<BR><LI>Press the <B>History</B> button<BR><LI>On the screen that appears, click the button that holds the name of the image you want to use (on the bottom of the window, you will see a text appear in the "Clipboard" field)<BR><LI>Go back to your forum message<BR><LI>Position the cursor inside your message where you want the image to appear<BR><LI>Press <B>CTL-V</B> (the same text as earlier in the "Clipboard" field will now appear in your message)<BR><LI> Press <B>Submit Reply</B><BR></UL><BR>The pasted text will now be replaced by your image!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||1
